.TH JANUSGATE-SETUP 8 "August 2026" "JanusGate 0.2.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
janusgate-setup \- initialize a JanusGate appliance safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B janusgate-setup --config
.I file
.RB ( --confirm-network | --image-build )
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ --no-enable-services ]
.br
.B janusgate-setup --config
.I file
.B --validate-only
.RI [ --image-build ]
.br
.B janusgate-setup --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B janusgate-setup
validates a bounded first-boot JSON document and initializes service
identities, private state directories, the database, the TOTP key, the server
identity, and service enablement.
Operations are ordered so an invalid document cannot partially configure the
appliance.
.PP
The configuration file must be a regular file owned by the invoking user and
must not be writable by group or other users.
Unknown JSON members and embedded null bytes are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Read the complete first-boot JSON document from
.IR file .
.TP
.B --confirm-network
Confirm that the named ingress, egress, and management interfaces have been
physically verified on this host.
.TP
.B --image-build
Permit configured interface names that are absent while constructing an
offline image.
.TP
.B --validate-only
Validate the document and host assumptions without changing state.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the ordered setup actions without changing state.
.TP
.B --no-enable-services
Complete initialization but leave installed services disabled.
.TP
.B --help
Display the complete command synopsis and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display build version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The top-level object contains
.BR network ,
.BR certificate ,
and
.B enable_services
members.
The network object declares four distinct interface names, bridge MTU,
packet-queue range and length, failure mode, STP, multicast snooping, and CPU
fanout.
The certificate object either identifies an existing PEM source or requests a
new local identity with a common name, alternative names, and bounded validity.
.PP
The installed OpenBSD example selects one fail-closed queue and disables CPU
fanout, multicast-snooping control, and explicit bridge MTU changes.
.PP
See
.I /etc/janusgate/janusgate.conf.example
for the complete schema-shaped example.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/janusgate.conf.example
Installed example setup document.
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/certs/server.pem
Installed or newly created server identity.
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/janusgate.db
Initialized persistent appliance state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/totp.key
New appliance-local TOTP protection key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validation or initialization completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Validation, privilege, filesystem, database, certificate, or service
processing failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SECURITY
Run setup from a trusted local console.
Review interface roles before using
.BR --confirm-network .
Protect the setup document if it refers to private certificate material.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR janusgatectl (1),
.BR janusgated (8),
.BR janusgate-netd (8),
.BR janusgate-web (8)
